    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What is measured and what is missing",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Current accounts and distinct verified users: not available.** Neither the identity database nor the Admin API is queried. A successful registration, an email verification and an existing account are different quantities.\n\nCounters describe observed, confirmed activity, including tests that use the same paths. They are neither organic adoption nor durable historical totals, and values are estimates that can be fractional. Seven-day estimates can cover less history because of retention, restarts or collection gaps. “Today” uses Europe/Madrid; trends use rolling 24-hour windows. Zero is only valid when the source is configured and healthy.\n\n**Milestones of 10 cumulative rating creations: pending a durable source and reliable exclusion of synthetic activity.** They are not simulated with Prometheus windows."
      }
    }
